cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use the released images, cite the dataset as well (see data/public_subset/CITATION.cff)."
title: "D2R: Two-Stage Diffusion and GAN Refinement for Heritage Image Inpainting"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a two-stage image restoration pipeline: LoRA
  fine-tuning of Stable Diffusion Inpainting (Stage 1), followed by texture-aware
  GAN residual refinement (Stage 2), with a matched end-to-end single-stage U-Net
  control. Includes the leakage-free input protocol, the evaluation harness and
  the budget/parameter accounting used in the accompanying manuscript.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
# Replace OWNER with your GitHub account or organisation before publishing.
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/d2r-inpainting"
keywords:
  - image inpainting
  - diffusion models
  - LoRA
  - generative adversarial network
  - cultural heritage
  - bronze mirrors
authors:
  - family-names: Guan
    given-names: Jun
  - family-names: Jia
    given-names: Qian
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Jianmin
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Yang
notes: >-
  Development status: unfinished research code under best-effort maintenance. Known
  defects, rough edges and the maintenance policy are listed in docs/STATUS.md; there
  is no API stability guarantee. All reported measurements are single-seed and are not
  final manuscript values. Accompanying manuscript: "Two-Stage Structural
  Reconstruction and Texture Refinement for Digital Restoration of Ancient Chinese
  Mountain-Pattern Bronze Mirror Photographs", npj Heritage Science, manuscript ID
  a062e16c-271f-4765-88b0-c2ef3985d848. The released image subset is licensed
  separately under CC0 1.0 Universal, is not covered by the software licence, and is
  a living collection that will grow as further image permissions are obtained.
